{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "```python\ndef _validate_array_length(array1: list, array2: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates that both arrays have equal length.\n    Returns True if lengths are equal, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    return len(array1) == len(array2)\n\ndef _check_element_relationship(elem1: any, elem2: any, elem3: any, elem4: any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if element pairs have the same equality relationship.\n    Returns True if (elem1 == elem2) is equivalent to (elem3 == elem4).\n    \"\"\"\n    return (elem1 == elem2) == (elem3 == elem4)\n\ndef _compare_patterns(array1: list, array2: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares element relationships between arrays to determine pattern match.\n    Iterates through all pairs of elements to check consistency.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array1)\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(n):\n            if not _check_element_relationship(array1[i], array1[j], array2[i], array2[j]):\n                return False\n    return True\n\ndef is_samepatterns(array1: list, array2: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point for pattern matching.\n    Checks if two arrays follow the same structural pattern.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_array_length(array1, array2):\n        return False\n    return _compare_patterns(array1, array2)\n```"}
