{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculate the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n\n    Args:\n        n: Position in sequence (positive integer)\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth Newman-Conway sequence value\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp[i] will store the i-th Newman-Conway number (1-indexed)\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[1] = 1\n    dp[2] = 1\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        dp[i] = dp[dp[i-1]] + dp[i - dp[i-1]]\n\n    return dp[n]"}
