{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "```python\ndef eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculate Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    This function computes a(n, m) using its standard mathematical definition.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _combinations(n_val: int, k_val: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient (n_val choose k_val).\"\"\"\n        if k_val < 0 or k_val > n_val:\n            return 0\n        if k_val == 0 or k_val == n_val:\n            return 1\n        if k_val > n_val // 2:\n            k_val = n_val - k_val\n\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(k_val):\n            res = res * (n_val - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    def _compute_eulerian_internal(n_val: int, m_val: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Internal computation logic for Eulerian numbers based on the formula.\"\"\"\n        if n_val == 0 and m_val == 0:\n            return 1\n        if m_val < 0 or m_val >= n_val:\n            return 0\n        \n        # Standard formula: sum_{k=0 to m} (-1)^k * C(n+1, k) * (m - k + 1)^n\n        result = 0\n        for k in range(m_val + 1):\n            term = ((-1)**k) * _combinations(n_val + 1, k) * ((m_val - k + 1)**n_val)\n            result += term\n        return result\n\n    return _compute_eulerian_internal(n, m)\n```"}
