{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Set\n\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists: List[List[int]]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find elements that appear in all sublists of the nested list.\n    Returns a list of integers common to all sublists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return []\n\n    common_elements_set: Set[int] = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    for sublist in nested_lists[1:]:\n        common_elements_set = common_elements_set.intersection(set(sublist))\n        if not common_elements_set:\n            break\n\n    return list(common_elements_set)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "```python\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"Find common elements across all sublists in nested lists.\n    It accepts nested lists of integers and returns common elements.\"\"\"\n    # Input validation.\n    if not nested_lists or not all(isinstance(sublist, list) for sublist in nested_lists):\n        return []\n\n    # Convert first sublist to set for intersection.\n    common_set = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Intersect with remaining sublists.\n    for sublist in nested_lists[1:]:\n        common_set = common_set.intersection(set(sublist))\n\n    # Return as list (set-compatible).\n    return list(common_set)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/113", "solution": "def _trim_whitespace(input_str: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes leading and trailing whitespace from a string.\"\"\"\n    return input_str.strip()\n\ndef _is_numeric(character: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a single character is a numeric digit '0' through '9'.\"\"\"\n    return '0' <= character <= '9'\n\ndef check_integer(string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string represents a valid integer, handling whitespace and a leading sign.\n    Returns True for valid integers, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not string:\n        return False\n\n    trimmed_string = _trim_whitespace(string)\n\n    if not trimmed_string:\n        return False\n\n    start_index = 0\n    if trimmed_string[0] == '-':\n        start_index = 1\n\n    # An empty string after handling a potential sign is not a valid integer (e.g., \"-\").\n    if len(trimmed_string) <= start_index:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(start_index, len(trimmed_string)):\n        if not _is_numeric(trimmed_string[i]):\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
