{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def _validate_input(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates if the input number is a positive integer.\"\"\"\n    return number > 0\n\ndef _check_binary_representation(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a positive number's binary form only uses non-zero powers of 2.\"\"\"\n    # A number is a sum of non-zero powers of two if and only if it's an even positive number.\n    # This implies its least significant bit (2^0) is not set.\n    return (number % 2 == 0)\n\ndef is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2.\n    For example, 10 (binary 1010) = 2^3 + 2^1 = 8 + 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_input(number):\n        return False\n    return _check_binary_representation(number)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def _validate_input(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validates that the input number is a positive integer.\"\"\"\n    return number > 0\n\ndef _check_power_sum(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a positive integer can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2.\n    This holds true for any positive even integer.\"\"\"\n    return number % 2 == 0\n\ndef is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a given number can be represented as a sum of non-zero powers of 2.\n    Non-zero powers of 2 are considered 2^k where k >= 1 (e.g., 2, 4, 8, ...).\"\"\"\n    if not _validate_input(number):\n        return False\n    \n    # 1 (which is 2^0) cannot be represented as a sum exclusively of powers 2^k where k >= 1.\n    if number == 1:\n        return False\n\n    return _check_power_sum(number)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "```python\ndef _count_zeros(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of zero values in an integer array.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for x in array:\n        if x == 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\ndef _count_non_zeros(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of non-zero values in an integer array.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for x in array:\n        if x != 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\ndef _calculate_ratio(zero_count: int, non_zero_count: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zero count to non-zero count, handling division by zero.\"\"\"\n    if non_zero_count == 0:\n        return float('inf')\n    return float(zero_count) / non_zero_count\n\ndef zero_count(array: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zero values to non-zero values in an integer array.\"\"\"\n    num_zeros = _count_zeros(array)\n    num_non_zeros = _count_non_zeros(array)\n    return _calculate_ratio(num_zeros, num_non_zeros)\n```"}
