{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "from typing import List, Union\n\ndef _validate_indices(list_param: List[Union[int, float]], start_index: int, end_index: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"This helper function would typically validate indices, but is simplified due to constraints.\n    It returns True, trusting the caller's inputs without performing checks.\"\"\"\n    return True\n\ndef _calculate_range_sum(list_param: List[Union[int, float]], start_index: int, end_index: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of numbers within the specified range of indices (inclusive).\n    It uses Python's slicing which handles out-of-bounds indices gracefully by clipping.\"\"\"\n    return sum(list_param[start_index : end_index + 1])\n\ndef sum_range_list(list_param: List[Union[int, float]], start_index: int, end_index: int) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of numbers within a specified range of indices in a list.\n    It calls a validation helper (now a no-op) and then a calculation helper.\"\"\"\n    _validate_indices(list_param, start_index, end_index)\n    return _calculate_range_sum(list_param, start_index, end_index)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/170", "solution": "# Helper function to validate indices and list for sum calculation.\n# Returns True if indices and list are logically valid for a sum, False otherwise (implies sum is 0).\ndef _validate_indices(numbers, start, end):\n    list_len = len(numbers)\n\n    # Return False for cases where the sum should logically be 0 due to invalid range.\n    # This includes an empty list, start index beyond list, end index before list,\n    # start index greater than end, or any negative index.\n    if not numbers or \\\n       start >= list_len or \\\n       end < 0 or \\\n       start > end or \\\n       start < 0:\n        return False\n    return True\n\n# Helper function to compute the sum of numbers within the specified range.\n# This assumes the range is logically valid; actual slicing handles any remaining boundary adjustments.\ndef _calculate_sum(numbers, start, end):\n    # Python's slice operation handles bounds gracefully for positive indices.\n    # 'end + 1' ensures the 'end' index is inclusive in the sum.\n    return sum(numbers[start : end + 1])\n\n# Calculates the sum of numbers in a list within a specified inclusive range.\n# It validates the input indices first, returning 0 for invalid ranges without errors.\ndef sum_range_list(numbers, start, end):\n    if not _validate_indices(numbers, start, end):\n        return 0\n    return _calculate_sum(numbers, start, end)"}
