{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "```python\n# Helper class for binary search operations.\nclass BinarySearcher:\n    \"\"\"\n    Implements binary search algorithms for finding element occurrences.\n    Provides methods to find the first and last occurrences of a target in a sorted array.\n    \"\"\"\n    def find_first_occurrence(self, arr: list, target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the index of the first occurrence of the target element in a sorted array.\n        Returns -1 if the target is not found.\n        \"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                high = mid - 1 # Try to find an earlier occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n    def find_last_occurrence(self, arr: list, target: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the index of the last occurrence of the target element in a sorted array.\n        Returns -1 if the target is not found.\n        \"\"\"\n        low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n        result = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                result = mid\n                low = mid + 1 # Try to find a later occurrence\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else: # arr[mid] > target\n                high = mid - 1\n        return result\n\n# Helper class for calculating the majority threshold.\nclass ThresholdCalculator:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the majority threshold based on the array's length.\n    Ensures calculations are robust for various input sizes.\n    \"\"\"\n    def calculate_majority_threshold(self, length: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the minimum count an element needs to be a majority element (n/2).\n        Uses integer division, effectively floor(n/2).\n        \"\"\"\n        return length // 2\n\ndef is_majority(array: list, n: int, element: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    Leverages binary search for O(log n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    binary_searcher = BinarySearcher()\n    threshold_calculator = ThresholdCalculator()\n\n    first_occurrence = binary_searcher.find_first_occurrence(array, element)\n\n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be the majority element.\n    if first_occurrence == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_occurrence = binary_searcher.find_last_occurrence(array, element)\n\n    # Calculate the total count of the element.\n    count = last_occurrence - first_occurrence + 1\n\n    # Calculate the majority threshold.\n    majority_threshold = threshold_calculator.calculate_majority_threshold(n)\n\n    # Check if the element's count exceeds the majority threshold.\n    return count > majority_threshold\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def validate_input(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"Handles specific edge cases where majority can be determined immediately.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False  # An empty array cannot have a majority element.\n    if n == 1:\n        return array[0] == element # Single element array: majority if it matches.\n    return None # Return None to indicate further processing is needed.\n\ndef binary_search_first(array, element, start, end):\n    \"\"\"Finds the first occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    result = -1\n    while start <= end:\n        mid = start + (end - start) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            end = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence.\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            start = mid + 1\n        else: # array[mid] > element\n            end = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef binary_search_last(array, element, start, end):\n    \"\"\"Finds the last occurrence of an element in a sorted array using binary search.\"\"\"\n    result = -1\n    while start <= end:\n        mid = start + (end - start) // 2\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid\n            start = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence.\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            start = mid + 1\n        else: # array[mid] > element\n            end = mid - 1\n    return result\n\ndef calculate_majority(first_index, last_index, n):\n    \"\"\"Determines if the count of occurrences exceeds n/2.\"\"\"\n    if first_index == -1: # Element not found at all.\n        return False\n    count = last_index - first_index + 1\n    return count > n / 2\n\ndef is_majority(array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates the majority detection algorithm for a sorted array.\n    Handles input validation, finds element occurrences, and checks for majority.\"\"\"\n\n    validation_result = validate_input(array, n, element)\n    if validation_result is not None:\n        return validation_result\n\n    first_idx = binary_search_first(array, element, 0, n - 1)\n    last_idx = binary_search_last(array, element, 0, n - 1)\n\n    return calculate_majority(first_idx, last_idx, n)"}
