{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\nfrom typing import Union\n\ndef _calculate_next_perfect_square(number: Union[int, float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the input number.\n    It determines the next integer whose square will exceed the given number.\"\"\"\n    candidate_root = math.sqrt(number)\n    # Find the smallest integer root whose square is greater than 'number'.\n    # For example, for 35 (sqrt ~5.91), floor is 5, next_root_int is 6.\n    # For 25 (sqrt 5.0), floor is 5, next_root_int is 6.\n    next_root_int = math.floor(candidate_root) + 1\n    return next_root_int * next_root_int\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: Union[int, float]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the given number.\n    This function delegates the core computation to an internal helper.\"\"\"\n    return _calculate_next_perfect_square(number)"}
