{"task_id": "Mbpp/252", "solution": "```python\nimport math\nfrom typing import Union, Tuple\n\ndef _extract_real_imaginary(complex_input: Union[complex, int, float]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Extract real and imaginary parts from input.\n    Converts input to a complex number first to handle all allowed types.\"\"\"\n    complex_val = complex(complex_input)\n    return float(complex_val.real), float(complex_val.imag)\n\ndef _calculate_magnitude(real: float, imaginary: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculate magnitude using Euclidean distance.\n    Uses math.sqrt for the calculation.\"\"\"\n    return math.sqrt(real**2 + imaginary**2)\n\ndef _calculate_angle(real: float, imaginary: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculate angle using atan2 function.\n    Returns angle in radians.\"\"\"\n    return math.atan2(imaginary, real)\n\ndef convert(complex_input: Union[complex, int, float]) -> Tuple[float, float]:\n    \"\"\"Convert complex number to polar coordinates.\n    Returns a tuple (magnitude, angle).\"\"\"\n    real, imaginary = _extract_real_imaginary(complex_input)\n    magnitude = _calculate_magnitude(real, imaginary)\n    angle = _calculate_angle(real, imaginary)\n    return magnitude, angle\n```"}
