{"task_id": "Mbpp/265", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\n\ndef _create_sublists(input_list: List[Any], n: int) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Create sublists by distributing elements based on their index modulo n.\n    Elements are appended to sublists maintaining their original relative order.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize n empty sublists, assuming n is a positive integer as per critical requirements.\n    sublists: List[List[Any]] = [[] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # Distribute elements to sublists based on index modulo n.\n    for i, element in enumerate(input_list):\n        sublists[i % n].append(element)\n\n    return sublists\n\ndef list_split(input_list: List[Any], n: int) -> List[List[Any]]:\n    \"\"\"Split input list into n sublists based on an nth element pattern.\n    Each sublist collects elements at specific offsets (0, n, 2n, etc.; 1, n+1, 2n+1, etc.).\n    \"\"\"\n    # As per critical requirements, no input validation is performed.\n    return _create_sublists(input_list, n)"}
