{"task_id": "Mbpp/271", "solution": "```python\n# even_power_sum/src/__init__.py\n# Package initialization file (empty)\n\n\n# even_power_sum/src/calculator.py\ndef generate_even_numbers(n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Generate first n even natural numbers.\n    It produces numbers like 2, 4, 6, ... up to n terms.\n    \"\"\"\n    return [2 * i for i in range(1, n + 1)]\n\ndef calculate_fifth_power(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Raise number to the fifth power.\n    This function computes number ** 5.\n    \"\"\"\n    return number ** 5\n\ndef sum_powered_numbers(numbers: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sum all numbers in the list.\n    It calculates the total sum of the given list of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(numbers)\n\n\n# even_power_sum/src/main.py\nfrom .calculator import generate_even_numbers, calculate_fifth_power, sum_powered_numbers\n\ndef even_Power_Sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculate sum of first n even numbers raised to fifth power.\n    It orchestrates generation, powering, and summing of numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    even_numbers = generate_even_numbers(n)\n    powered_numbers = [calculate_fifth_power(num) for num in even_numbers]\n    total_sum = sum_powered_numbers(powered_numbers)\n    return total_sum\n```"}
