{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "```python\n# src/utils/helpers.py\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef is_increasing(elements: List[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates strict increasing order in element sequence.\n    Returns True if elements are strictly increasing, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not elements or len(elements) == 1:\n        return True\n    for x in range(len(elements) - 1):\n        if elements[x] >= elements[x+1]:\n            return False\n    return True\n\ndef calculate_sum(elements: List[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes sum of integer sequence.\n    Returns the total sum of all elements in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n    return sum(elements)\n\n# src/algorithm/validation.py\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef validate_parameters(n: int, i: int, k: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates constraint k > i and basic parameter validity.\n    Ensures logical consistency of algorithm parameters.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k <= i:\n        raise ValueError(\"k must be greater than i.\")\n    return True\n\ndef validate_array_bounds(array: List[int], k: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Verifies array has sufficient length for k index access.\n    Prevents index out of bounds errors.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) <= k:\n        raise IndexError(f\"Array length {len(array)} is not sufficient for index k={k}.\")\n    return True\n\n# src/algorithm/subsequence.py\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef compute_prefix_dp(array: List[int], i: int) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes maximum sums of increasing subsequences from prefix.\n    Dynamic programming solution for prefix subsequences up to index i.\n    \"\"\"\n    # dp[x] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at array[x]\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    for current_idx in range(i + 1):\n        dp[current_idx] = array[current_idx] # Subsequence can be just the element itself\n        for prev_idx in range(current_idx):\n            if array[current_idx] > array[prev_idx]:\n                dp[current_idx] = max(dp[current_idx], dp[prev_idx] + array[current_idx])\n    return dp\n\ndef find_max_sum_with_kth(array: List[int], prefix_dp: List[int], i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds maximum sum including mandatory kth element.\n    Combines prefix results with kth element maintaining increasing order.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Initialize max_total_sum with the sum if only array[k] is the subsequence.\n    max_total_sum = array[k]\n\n    # Iterate through elements in the prefix (up to index i)\n    # to find an element array[x] that can precede array[k].\n    for x in range(i + 1):\n        if array[x] < array[k]:\n            # If array[x] is smaller than array[k], an increasing subsequence\n            # ending at array[x] can be extended with array[k].\n            max_total_sum = max(max_total_sum, prefix_dp[x] + array[k])\n    \n    return max_total_sum\n\n# src/main.py\nfrom typing import List\n# Assuming a flat import structure as per forbidden rules and overall response.\n# In a true file structure, these would be:\n# from src.algorithm.validation import validate_parameters, validate_array_bounds\n# from src.algorithm.subsequence import compute_prefix_dp, find_max_sum_with_kth\n\n# Re-defining functions or importing them if they are in the same code block.\n# Since the critical requirement states \"Every function you call must be defined inline in your response.\",\n# and the solution is presented as a single cohesive block, we can assume direct access.\n# If strict module imports were required for *this* presentation format, they would be as commented above.\n# For this response format, the functions are effectively \"inline\" globally.\n\ndef max_sum_increasing_subseq(array: List[int], n: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Main entry point orchestrating the complete algorithm.\n    Validates inputs and coordinates computation of maximum sum.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Interface Layer & Validation Layer\n    validate_parameters(n, i, k)\n    validate_array_bounds(array, k)\n\n    # 2. Algorithm Layer\n    # Compute DP for the prefix up to index i\n    prefix_dp = compute_prefix_dp(array, i)\n\n    # Find the maximum sum by combining prefix results with the mandatory kth element\n    max_sum = find_max_sum_with_kth(array, prefix_dp, i, k)\n\n    return max_sum\n```"}
