{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "```python\ndef set_left_most_unset_bit(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit in an integer's binary representation.\n    It finds the most significant zero bit within the number's length and flips it to one.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Determine the position of the most significant bit (MSB).\n    msb_pos = number.bit_length() - 1\n\n    # Iterate from the MSB position downwards to find the first unset bit.\n    for i in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        if ((number >> i) & 1) == 0:\n            # If the bit is 0, set it using a bitwise OR with a mask.\n            return number | (1 << i)\n\n    # If all bits from MSB down to 0 are set, set the bit immediately to the left of the MSB.\n    return number | (1 << (msb_pos + 1))\n```"}
