{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number iteratively.\n    It follows L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n)=L(n-1)+L(n-2) for n >= 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 2, 1  # L(0), L(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "```python\ndef find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the n'th Lucas number based on L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n)=L(n-1)+L(n-2).\n    It computes the number iteratively for non-negative integer inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n    \n    a, b = 2, 1  # Represents L(0) and L(1) initially\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b\n```"}
