{"task_id": "Mbpp/437", "solution": "```python\ndef remove_odd(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove characters at odd positions (1-based indexing) from input string.\n\n    Args:\n        input_string (str): The input string to process\n\n    Returns:\n        str: String containing only characters from even positions\n\n    Example:\n        >>> remove_odd(\"python\")\n        'yhn'\n    \"\"\"\n    result_chars = []\n    for i in range(len(input_string)):\n        # A 0-based index 'i' corresponds to a 1-based position of 'i + 1'.\n        # If 'i + 1' is even, then 'i' must be odd.\n        if i % 2 != 0:\n            result_chars.append(input_string[i])\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/437", "solution": "def remove_odd(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes characters at odd 1-indexed positions from the input string.\n    Returns a new string with characters from even 1-indexed positions.\"\"\"\n    \n    result_chars = []\n    # Characters at 0-indexed odd positions correspond to 1-indexed even positions.\n    for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n        if i % 2 != 0:  # Keep characters whose 0-indexed position is odd\n            result_chars.append(char)\n            \n    return \"\".join(result_chars)"}
