{"task_id": "Mbpp/462", "solution": "```python\ndef _validate_input(input_list: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Validate that input is a proper list. Always returns True as per requirements.\"\"\"\n    return True\n\ndef _build_subset(input_list: list, binary_mask: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Build individual subset based on binary mask.\n    Elements are added by prepending if their corresponding bit is set, matching specific output order.\n    \"\"\"\n    subset = []\n    n = len(input_list)\n    for i in range(n):\n        # Check if the i-th bit of the mask is set (from LSB upwards)\n        if (binary_mask >> i) & 1:\n            # Prepend the element to maintain the specific output order as per the example.\n            subset.insert(0, input_list[i])\n    return subset\n\ndef _generate_binary_combinations(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate combinations using a binary counting approach.\n    It iterates through all possible binary masks and builds subsets using helper.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    num_combinations = 1 << n  # Calculate 2^n\n    all_subsets = []\n    for mask in range(num_combinations):\n        all_subsets.append(_build_subset(input_list, mask))\n    return all_subsets\n\ndef combinations_list(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generate all possible combinations (subsets) of input list elements.\n    Returns: List of lists containing all possible subsets in binary counting order.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_input(input_list)\n    return _generate_binary_combinations(input_list)\n```"}
