{"task_id": "Mbpp/572", "solution": "def two_unique_nums(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Remove duplicate numbers from list, returning only numbers that appear exactly once.\n    This function preserves the original order of unique elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for num in input_list:\n        counts[num] = counts.get(num, 0) + 1\n\n    result = []\n    for num in input_list:\n        if counts[num] == 1:\n            result.append(num)\n\n    return result"}
