{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "```python\ndef armstrong_number(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number equals the sum of its own digits each raised to the power of the number of digits.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to count the number of digits in an integer.\n    def _count_digits(n: int) -> int:\n        return len(str(n))\n\n    # Helper function to extract individual digits from an integer into a list.\n    def _extract_digits(n: int) -> list[int]:\n        return [int(d) for d in str(n)]\n\n    # Helper function to calculate the sum of each digit raised to the specified power.\n    def _calculate_sum_of_powers(digits: list[int], power: int) -> int:\n        total_sum = 0\n        for digit in digits:\n            total_sum += digit ** power\n        return total_sum\n\n    # Main logic of the armstrong_number function.\n    # Input validation for positive integers is assumed to be handled by the caller as per requirements.\n    num_digits = _count_digits(number)\n    digits = _extract_digits(number)\n    calculated_sum = _calculate_sum_of_powers(digits, num_digits)\n    \n    return calculated_sum == number\n```"}
