{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "```python\ndef get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extract all adjacent coordinates in 3x3 grid pattern.\n    Calculates 9 coordinates including the original using -1, 0, +1 offsets.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate_tuple\n    offsets = [-1, 0, 1]\n    \n    result = []\n    for offset_x in offsets:\n        for offset_y in offsets:\n            new_x = x + offset_x\n            new_y = y + offset_y\n            result.append([new_x, new_y])\n            \n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def _generate_grid_offsets():\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates the 3x3 grid offset patterns.\n    These offsets define the relative positions around a center point in row-major order.\n    \"\"\"\n    offsets = []\n    for dy in [-1, 0, 1]:\n        for dx in [-1, 0, 1]:\n            offsets.append((dx, dy))\n    return offsets\n\ndef _calculate_adjacent_coordinates(x, y, offsets):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates actual coordinates from a center point (x, y) and a list of offsets.\n    Each offset (dx, dy) is added to the center (x, y) to find a new coordinate.\n    \"\"\"\n    adjacent_coords = []\n    for dx, dy in offsets:\n        adjacent_coords.append([x + dx, y + dy])\n    return adjacent_coords\n\ndef get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple):\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all adjacent coordinates in a 3x3 grid pattern, including the center.\n    Returns a list of coordinate pairs in row-major order.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate_tuple\n    offsets = _generate_grid_offsets()\n    return _calculate_adjacent_coordinates(x, y, offsets)"}
