{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(array: list, target_value) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the rightmost insertion point for a specified value in a sorted array.\n    This uses a binary search algorithm, achieving O(log n) time and O(1) space complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array)\n    ans = len(array) # Default insertion point if target_value is greater than all elements.\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] > target_value:\n            # array[mid] is a potential rightmost insertion point, or we can find an even smaller index.\n            ans = mid\n            high = mid\n        else:\n            # array[mid] <= target_value, so we need to search in the right half\n            # to find an element strictly greater than target_value.\n            low = mid + 1\n    return ans"}
