{"task_id": "Mbpp/797", "solution": "```python\ndef _is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given integer is an odd number.\n    It checks if the number has a non-zero remainder when divided by 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    return number % 2 != 0\n\ndef _validate_range(l: int, r: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Validates that range parameters are natural numbers and in correct order.\n    Returns True if l and r are positive integers and l is not greater than r.\n    \"\"\"\n    return l >= 1 and r >= 1 and l <= r\n\ndef sum_in_range(l: int, r: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of all odd natural numbers within the inclusive range [l, r].\n    It returns 0 if the range is invalid or contains no odd natural numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not _validate_range(l, r):\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for number in range(l, r + 1):\n        if _is_odd(number):\n            total_sum += number\n    return total_sum\n```"}
