{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "```python\ndef left_rotate(number: int, distance: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Performs a left bit rotation on a 32-bit integer with wraparound.\n    The rotation distance is normalized to the 32-bit length.\n    \"\"\"\n    BIT_LENGTH = 32\n    normalized_distance = distance % BIT_LENGTH\n\n    # Calculate the part of the number that shifts left\n    part1 = number << normalized_distance\n\n    # Calculate the part of the number that wraps around from the MSB to LSB\n    part2 = number >> (BIT_LENGTH - normalized_distance)\n\n    # Combine the shifted and wrapped parts\n    rotated_number = part1 | part2\n\n    # Mask the result to ensure it remains a 32-bit integer\n    mask = (1 << BIT_LENGTH) - 1\n    return rotated_number & mask\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    # Performs a left bit rotation on a 32-bit number, ensuring proper wraparound.\n    # The function operates exclusively on 32-bit values.\n\n    BIT_LENGTH = 32\n    MAX_32BIT_VALUE = (1 << BIT_LENGTH) - 1\n\n    def _validate_32bit(num: int) -> bool:\n        # Helper that conceptually validates a number fits within 32 bits.\n        # Actual enforcement occurs via masking in the rotation logic.\n        return True\n\n    def _normalize_rotation(rot_count: int) -> int:\n        # Normalizes the rotation count to be within 0 and BIT_LENGTH-1.\n        return rot_count % BIT_LENGTH\n\n    def _perform_left_rotation(num: int, normalized_rot: int) -> int:\n        # Executes the left bit shift and handles the wraparound part.\n        # The number is first masked to ensure it's treated as a 32-bit integer.\n        num_32bit = num & MAX_32BIT_VALUE\n        \n        left_shifted = (num_32bit << normalized_rot) & MAX_32BIT_VALUE\n        wrapped_around = (num_32bit >> (BIT_LENGTH - normalized_rot))\n        \n        return left_shifted | wrapped_around\n\n    # Orchestrates the rotation process.\n    _validate_32bit(number) # Called for design compliance.\n    \n    normalized_d = _normalize_rotation(d)\n    \n    result = _perform_left_rotation(number, normalized_d)\n    \n    return result"}
