{"task_id": "Mbpp/809", "solution": "```python\ndef check_smaller(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Compares elements of two tuples: returns True if every element in the second is smaller than its corresponding element in the first.\n    Returns False immediately if any element in the second tuple is greater than or equal to its corresponding element.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Assumes tuple1 and tuple2 have equal lengths as per the design specification and critical constraints.\n    for elem1, elem2 in zip(tuple1, tuple2):\n        if elem2 >= elem1:\n            return False\n    return True\n```"}
